==English==
{{wp}}
{{wikiquote}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|polythéisme}}, from {{der|en|grc|πολύς|t=many}} and {{m|grc|θεός|t=god}}, corresponding to {{af|en|poly-|theism}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɒl.ɪˈθiː.ɪz.əm/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-polytheism.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The belief in the existence of multiple [[god]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1734|tlr=w:en:George Sale|title=Alcoran of Mohammed|section=|passage= And remember when Lokmân said unto his son, as he admonished him, Oh my son, give not a partner unto GOD; for '''polytheism''' is a great impiety.}}
# A [[religion]] or [[belief]] system with multiple gods.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1941|author=George Ryley Scott|authorlink=George Ryley Scott|title=Phallic Worship: A History of Sex and Sex Rites in Relation to the Religions of All Races from Antiquity to the Present Day|publisher=T. Werner Laurie|location=London|page=14|passage=The Chaldeans worshipped the seven planets. These seven planets were the "Seven Great Gods" of the ancients, and constituted a '''polytheism''', the component members of which varied in importance, with the moon occupying the premier position.}}

